i get asked about the topic  of podcasts quite a bit mostly from my  youtube viewers and many of them will  say oh man i love this content could you  put this into a podcaster why don't you  have a  podcast already i'd like to have these  as downloadable  mp3s so i don't have to like keep  streaming your  content using a bandwidth and the answer  is  i actually do have a podcast it's called  sadler's lectures for the time being i  may change the name later  but that's basically what it is i  started it back  in may of 2018  and i've been putting out content and  regularly posting about it  in my social media that is in my twitter  stream  uh in my facebook page  and in linkedin really since that time  and when i first started out i was maybe  doing 10 episodes a month  now i'm up to releasing podcast episodes  almost daily so there's there's you know  over 350 tracks at this point in time  a lot of content and so you know i'd  invite you the link is is right below in  the video description if you're  interested  in my podcast but you haven't already  found out about it or listened to it  just go right there  on soundcloud you can also find it in a  variety of other  formats and platforms like apple  music and whatever google play is now  and a bunch of other things i've even  found by doing searches  that the podcast is aggregated in places  that i  i've never even heard of so it's out  there you just gotta  look for it but again you can go  straight to soundcloud and  find it there if that's what you want to  do so  i'm going to talk a little bit about the  podcast what i'm doing at present  and what i'd really like to do in the  future and you might  want to support that i'll talk more  about that at the end  so sandler's lectures i started taking  some of my philosophical core concept  videos and i've got  probably about 800 of them now and  i would take the the the video file turn  it into a sound file  the ones that i've shot more recently  where i'm using this voice recorder i  just use the voice recorder file  that makes it a lot more useful and then  i try to improve the sound as best as i  can  in some cases there's not that much that  you can do with it  in other cases there's quite a lot i'm  using audacity  which i'm comfortable with i don't want  to try to you know  invest in some really high-end digital  editing software because that's that's  you know not my shtick  right and then i take out all of the  ums and oz and places where i say a word  twice  and long pauses and sounds of me writing  on the blackboard  at least i try to get all that stuff out  of there and then i  you know tack on a little intro and a  little outro and there you got a podcast  episode  so i have been doing that actually i had  my  my daughter helping me out with that at  first but she wasn't really that into  it so i've been doing it myself since  uh 2018 and i've you know put out quite  a few i put together a list  of the different thinkers and this may  not include all of them  but the episodes that are available now  include heraclitus permanentes  plato aristotle epicurus cicero  seneca epictetus augustine anselm  descartes pascal  hume bentham kant hegel mill  kierkegaard dostoyevsky nietzsche marcel  sartre bouvoir camus james  rilke air rawls kohlberg singer  a rant and and i think i probably left  some people off of that  as well and i've also got a few  talks that i gave here and there one  comes to mind the talk that i gave  at the marquette aristotle conference  about thumbos  and its history that's that spirited  part of the soul  i recorded that as i was giving it and i  converted it into a podcast episode and  i'll probably do that with  others in the future so if you go to the  podcast  and you kind of just look around you're  going to find  lectures anywhere from like  8 minutes at the shortest to 30 minutes  at the longest  on all of these different thinkers and  some other key works  it is the same content basically as  you're going to find in core concept  videos  so you know nothing absolutely new there  but  people find them very very helpful and i  use this content  in my online classes i provide it as a  resource to students so you know they  can download it  have it on their phone they go to the  gym they take a walk they're driving  working out whatever they can listen to  me talking about  you know rene descartes and what's going  on in the meditations or  you know about cicero and his different  views on the stoics or the epicureans or  whatever it  happens to be it's totally up to them  so i use these as resources for my own  students  i also provide them to my clients  you know i have a lot of individual  clients and if they're interested in  something i shoot those  podcast episodes to them i say here  check check these resources out right  but the general public seems to be quite  interested in them  and find them useful as well i think  that just a lot of people don't  don't know about them they know about me  more for the youtube videos  and perhaps less for the podcast  episodes  i did go through and take a look at the  stats  and i was pleasantly surprised to find  out  that um all told since the inception  i've had about 140 000  uh listens to to these and you know i  i'm sure that's counting ones that are  coming through  other um formats and platforms as well  but just in the last year in 2020  we had over 100 000 plays  of this this podcast content which is  really gratifying and in december  december was a really bumper month we  had  over 14 000 so getting some traction  i do want to thank one particular  twitter you know user who generates a  lot of cool stuff  and that's true sci-fi that's that's  kelly true love  and you know the the putting  the lists together and having the uh  featuring in the channel that's been  really helpful i  imagine in spreading the word but i do  want to get the word out there a little  bit more which is why i'm shooting this  video the last thing that i  i would like to talk about is  people say okay so you've got a podcast  you're doing these saddlers lectures  that's really nice  um you know you can you i can get this  content elsewhere it's not really  original content because it's  your youtube videos granted it's better  quality  and they're a little bit shorter to  listen to because you took out all of  your you knows  and likes and words like that  when are you going to start doing like  original  podcast content and there's two answers  to that one  is i have done a lot of original podcast  content it's just  basically on other people's podcasts  i've gone on  to so many other people's podcasts  video channels hybrids of the two that  i've got a very long  list of guest appearances i've i've also  done some guest  hosting for example for the sunday stoic  podcast recently  and you could count the wisdom for life  podcast as something  that i do that's the radio show that i  do with with dan hayes here in milwaukee  running every saturday uh while kovit is  going on and then we might go back to  friday times once once we're out of that  so there's all of that right i'm on  podcasts but  you know when it comes to shooting  original podcast or  rather recording original podcast  content  i'm going to do that when i reach a  higher level of  patreon support why because you know i'm  a busy guy  and creating original podcast content  that  that takes a lot of work and a lot of  time and i would need to divert  some time from the other things i'm  doing to creating  that content for people so if if you  want to see that the  key thing to do is to you know support  on patreon i'm going to put a link to  that below  as well and if you like my other stuff  that i do like videos and blog posting  and the public events that i host  online worldwide you might consider  becoming a patreon supporter as well  even if it's at just the one dollar  level give back a little bit  right if you're getting some value out  of the stuff that i do but so podcasting  it is something that i i'm looking  forward eventually to getting into  in a more original way for the time  being it's going to be these  sadler's lectures which people seem to  enjoy  so i'm going to keep cranking them out  and they're really helpful resources  for my philosophy students so i kind of  get a  you know double dip that way so long  story short you know going back to the  key question  hey dr sather why don't you turn these  lectures into podcast episodes or  why don't you have a podcast the answer  is i already have been doing that  link is below you can go and check it  out hope you enjoy it  you

